  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3edf825c44ba8994197fd4cca4373a22, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Hello, my friend,


    May I call you that now? Lin Wei here.


    Kung
    pao chicken is loud food. Chili, peanuts, a hot wok shouting at you. My wife
    says it is the only time I raise my voice.


    Cut the chicken small, toast
    the chilies until they darken but never burn, and add the peanuts last so they
    stay crisp.


    When your shop gets busy and noisy, do not be afraid of it.
    A loud kitchen is a living kitchen.'
